        {
          "name": "process.poll",
          "description": "Wait up to timeout milliseconds for a background process session started by exec to produce new output or exit, then return its state. The reply carries the session status, exit code and signal, failure kind, the stdout and stderr produced since the last poll (deltas are consumed and returned once), elapsed milliseconds, total output characters, whether output was truncated, and a tail excerpt of recent output. timeout defaults to 1000 and is clamped to 0-120000; 0 returns the current state immediately. Backgrounded exec commands deliver their terminal result into your context automatically, so never poll just to wait for completion; if a finished session's completion message is already queued for automatic delivery, this call returns an error instead of double-reporting it. For the full accumulated log use process.log; to stop the process use process.kill.",
