          "description": "Send named key presses to a background process session started by exec, encoded as terminal control sequences and written to the session's input. Intended for PTY sessions running interactive programs. keys is an ordered list of case-insensitive tokens: enter or return, tab, escape or esc, space, backspace, up, down, left, right, home, end, pageup, pagedown, insert, delete, f1 through f12, and control chords written c-<char> (for example c-c, c-d, c-z). An unsupported token fails the whole call and nothing is sent. Set eof true to close the session's input after the keys. The reply reports the session id, bytes written, and whether input was closed. For plain text use process.write; to see the program's response, follow with process.poll.",
