          "name": "chat.create",
          "description": "Create a new side chat, a separate persistent Muse conversation alongside the main chat. A side chat is always a private 1:1 conversation between you and this user. This is not a group chat and there is no way to add other people. context_mode is required: use \"fork\" when the current main chat's history is relevant to the new chat, so it starts with that context, or \"fresh\" when it should start without previous conversation context. Forking is only allowed from the main chat; creating a forked side chat from a side chat is rejected. Optionally set name, a short human-readable title of at most 120 characters. The optional message field is context about what the chat is for: when no name is given it seeds an automatically generated title. It is not delivered into the new chat as a message; to actually give the new chat's agent something to do, follow up with chat.send_message. Returns the new chat's chat_id.",
